course: dictionary
lesson: 6798
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer means. «Great Britain's national mapping agency, Ordnance Survey, began in 1791 and makes detailed maps at scales of 1:25,000 and 1:50,000.» Here ordnance is part of a name, and the clues are mapping, maps and scales, so it means the map-making organisation.
explain: On its own, ordnance means military weapons, especially large guns, bombs, shells and ammunition. Ask what the nearby words are about: war and battles, or maps and land. That question tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Always check your choice by putting it into the sentence. Does «the army fired its ordnance» make sense? Yes, it means the army fired its big guns. Does «Ordnance Survey makes detailed maps» make sense? Yes, so it is the mapping organisation.
fact: Ordnance means military weapons, especially large guns, bombs, shells and ammunition.
fact: Ordnance Survey is the government map-making organisation of Great Britain, and Ordnance Survey Ireland does the same job in Ireland.
fact: Ordnance is uncountable, so you say some ordnance, not an ordnance.
fact: «Unexploded ordnance» means old bombs or shells that have not gone off, and they can still be found on beaches and building sites.
fact: Ordnance Survey maps are detailed maps that use grid references, which help you find a place quickly.
exercise: «Great Britain's national mapping agency, Ordnance Survey, began in 1791.» What does Ordnance Survey do? | Fires large guns in battles | Stores bombs and shells in the army | Clears old ammunition from beaches | *Makes detailed maps
exercise: In a history lesson, a teacher says «unexploded ordnance» was found on a building site. What does ordnance mean here? | Bricks and wood for building | Detailed maps of the land | Small toys for children | *Old bombs or shells that have not gone off
exercise: In the sentence about Ordnance Survey, find one word that tells you the meaning is about maps. | 1791 | Britain's | began | *maps
test: What does ordnance mean in a war story? | Maps of the battlefield | Soldiers' boots and coats | Brave people who fight | *Large guns, bombs, shells and ammunition
test: In «Ordnance Survey makes detailed maps», what does Ordnance Survey mean? | A battle fought in 1791 | A type of large gun | A school for soldiers | *The government map-making organisation
exam: Jayden sees ordnance in a history book and on an OS map; how can he tell which meaning is which? | Skip it, it never matters | Guess at random | Ask for a new book | *Check the clue words nearby, such as war or maps
